    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-in-film-production-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Film Production",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor in Film Production - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor in Film Production Assistant Teaching Professor in Film Production 499896 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Oct 6 2026 Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Overview The Film and Television Arts Program in the Department of Theatre, Film and Creative Writing at Boise State University invites applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor in Film Production, beginning Fall 2027. Film and Television Arts is a relatively new program and is currently one of the fastest-growing on campus. The successful candidate will teach fundamental and advanced film production, as well as at least two intermediate skills courses (e.g., Directing, Cinematography, Sound Design, Post-Production with Adobe Creative Cloud, and Producing). The ability to teach Film Audio, Animation, and/or Documentary will receive additional consideration. The selected candidate will teach four (4) classes per semester (Fall & Spring) and contribute 20% of their time to service to the university and community. Department Overview The Department of Theatre, Film, and Creative Writing is situated in the School of the Arts—an academic unit designed to serve as a vibrant urban hub for the study, practice, and integration of the arts. The School cultivates new models of interdisciplinary innovation, entrepreneurial initiative, and collaborative community engagement to prepare artists and students to thrive in a diverse world. About Boise State Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital—a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We are nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop—a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, a growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Minimum Qualifications MFA or equivalent terminal degree in film production or a related discipline or graduate degree with commensurate professional experience. Professional background and experience in areas such as narrative production, documentary, or commercial projects. College-level teaching experience from foundational through advanced levels. Preferred Qualifications Professional experience and ability to teach multiple areas of film production and/or postproduction. Track-record of full-time academic teaching. Demonstrated knowledge of professional media software and hardware. Expertise with Mac post-production workflows and Adobe Creative Cloud. Desire to contribute to a growing Film program. Required Application Materials Cover letter detailing teaching philosophy. Curriculum Vitae (CV). Link to a professional portfolio or demo reel. Contact information for three references. Closing Date The position will close to new applicants on November 6th. Contact Information For questions regarding this position, please contact Ru Wood: Email: rulonwood@boisestate.edu Salary and Benefits Salary starts at $58,656 and is commensurate with experience. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract. More information about faculty contract and work-days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): ●      10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) ●      Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages ● Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents ● Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. ●      See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) b276342c Last Name (required) 033f7c58 Email (required) a1b0e8df Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and 