    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/provost-and-vice-president-for-academic-affairs-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs",
      "description": "Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs 499822 Boise, Idaho Faculty Non-Classified/Professional Opening on: Aug 24 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Boise State University seeks a strategic, forward-looking academic leader to serve as its next Provost and Vice President for Academic Affairs. Reporting directly to the President, the Provost serves as the university's Chief Academic Officer and plays a central role in shaping and advancing Boise State's academic, research, and student success priorities. As Idaho's largest public university, Boise State serves more than 28,500 students and offers a broad portfolio of undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs. Over the past several years, the institution has experienced record enrollment growth, significant increases in student retention and graduation rates, and substantial expansion in research productivity and doctoral education. A metropolitan research university deeply connected to the economic and workforce needs of Idaho, Boise State has emerged as a national model for integrating student success, innovation, community engagement, and applied research, while positioning itself for Carnegie R1 research university classification. At a time of significant change across higher education and within the university, Boise State seeks a provost who can build trust, foster collaboration, and strengthen relationships across the university community. The successful candidate will demonstrate a commitment to transparent communication, shared governance, and thoughtful leadership that balances innovation with institutional stability. Boise State has experienced significant growth in research activity, doctoral education, enrollment, and national visibility, establishing itself as one of the nation's rising public universities. The next Provost will help shape the institution's next chapter, building on this momentum to advance student success, expand scholarly impact, strengthen academic quality, and foster innovation across the university. Working closely with the President, deans, faculty, and university leadership, the Provost will guide the continued evolution of Boise State as a premier student-success driven, public research university. This includes advancing innovation in teaching and learning; strengthening alignment among academic programs, workforce needs, research and creative activity, and community impact; stewarding resources in support of academic priorities and long-term sustainability; and articulating the value of a Boise State education for students, families, and the state of Idaho. Boise State seeks an accomplished academic leader with an earned doctorate or terminal degree, a record of scholarly achievement meriting appointment as a full professor, and significant senior leadership experience. The ideal candidate will demonstrate a strong commitment to shared governance, academic excellence, research growth, faculty engagement, and student success, along with the strategic vision, operational expertise, and collaborative leadership necessary to guide a complex public university through a period of continued growth and opportunity. All applications, nominations, and inquiries are invited. Applications should include, as two separate documents, a CV and a letter of interest addressing the themes in the leadership profile. WittKieffer is assisting Boise State University in this search. For fullest consideration, candidate materials should be received by November 13, 2026. Application materials should be submitted using WittKieffer's candidate portal . Nominations and inquiries can be directed to: Zachary A. Smith, Ph.D., Lauren Bruce-Stets, and Tyler Workman at BoiseStateProvost@wittkieffer.com . Back to job search Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 093242c0 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Academic Affairs Administration and Business Operations Senior-Level Academic Affairs Administration and Business Operations Senior-Level Employment Type Faculty Non-Classified/Professional Faculty Non-Classified/Professional Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 791fe115 Last Name (required) 3c009584 Email (required) 40eb2a9a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
