    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-of-cellular-and-molecular-biology-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Cellular and Molecular Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Cellular and Molecular Biology - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Professor of Cellular and Molecular Biology Assistant Professor of Cellular and Molecular Biology 499872 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Sep 25 2026 Closing on: Oct 26 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Biological Sciences at Boise State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor with expertise in Cellular and Molecular Biology. We are seeking candidates who share our commitment to research and teaching. The new hire will be expected to develop an externally funded research program that supports graduate student training. The new hire will contribute to existing courses or develop new courses within their expertise, including experiential learning opportunities. We offer dedicated laboratory space, start-up funds and access to shared instrumentation and core facilities. Graduate student assistantships in interdisciplinary Ph.D. programs in Biomolecular Sciences and in Computing are available to support the mentoring of Ph.D. students. This position is part of Boise State University's interdisciplinary Biomolecular Sciences Cluster Hire Initiative, with open positions in the departments of Biological Sciences, Chemistry & Biochemistry, Mathematics, and Physics. The goal is to support a cohort of scientists with the potential to create new interdisciplinary research collaborations, support graduate education and the growth of doctoral programs, position Boise State for long-term research distinction, and build on existing institutional strengths. We strongly encourage applications from candidates whose research has biomedical applications and strong potential to attract NIH and other externally sponsored research funding. In addition to describing the funding potential of planned research, candidates should describe the potential for their research to contribute to at least one of the existing or emerging areas of interdisciplinary strength at Boise State University, including Matrix Biology COBRE , the Convergent Engineering and Biomolecular Science (CEBS) COBRE , Healthy Idaho Clinical and Translational Research (CTR-D) Program , Food and Dairy Innovation Center , Neuroscience , Cancer Research, or Quantum Information Science. Applicants should also discuss how their research could leverage Boise State's shared instrumentation, core facilities (BRCF and FaCT Cores), and collaborative research infrastructure, including resources available through the Biomedical Research Institute , while also contributing to a collaborative environment that advances scientific discovery, graduate education, and externally funded research. Department overview: The Department of Biological Sciences at Boise State University holds a strong commitment to research, teaching and service. Our department serves over 600 students majoring in biology, and many more students taking biology courses for other degree programs. We share teaching experiences and strategies in order to improve the experiences of our students. Our faculty members contribute to several graduate programs at the PhD and Masters level and we take pride in mentoring our graduate students within these programs. Our department is committed to the success of our faculty and provides both informal and formal mentoring to support career development. Research in our department spans all levels of biological sciences creating numerous opportunities for collaboration and growth. In addition, our faculty frequently collaborate with faculty across the University and at other institutions. The Department of Biological Sciences offers a flexible workload policy that allows a balance of research and teaching that is appropriate for career stage and interests. Faculty with high levels of research activity typically teach the equivalent of 1 class each semester (1:1 teaching workload). In the first year, faculty are typically offered a reduced teaching and service workload. Faculty have access to a state-of-the-art rodent vivarium and zebrafish facility, the Biomolecular Research Core (BRC), shared spaces in the Department of Biological Sciences, and additional core facilities across campus. Two distinct NIH funded Centers of Biomedical Research Excellence (COBRE), one in Matrix Biology and one in Convergent Engineering and Biomolecular Sciences (CEBS), are located within the Biomedical Research Institute. Research core facilities have full-time dedicated staff to maintain instrumentation, provide training, and perform services. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: A PhD in a field related to the Biological Sciences Preferred qualifications: A record of research accomplishment appropriate to the candidate’s career stage, including peer-reviewed publications and experience pursuing extramural funding. Experience mentoring undergraduate students, graduate students, or postdoctoral researchers. A promising research agenda with potential for NIH or other extramural funding. Research that aligns with one or more of the interdisciplinary research strengths described in the position overview. Potential to use and contribute to Boise State’s CORE facilities. Evidence of effective teaching and a commitment to continued growth as an instructor. Evidence of effective student mentoring and support for student learning. Required application materials: 1) Cover Letter describing your interest in the position and the contributions you would make to the Department of Biological Sciences at Boise State University. 2) Curriculum Vitae that includes employment history with dates, publications, grant activity, courses taught, student mentoring, leadership roles and responsibilities, service, and other relevant professional activities. 3) Research Statement (two pages maximum), describing: Your research accomplishments and experience with extramural funding; Your future research agenda and its potential for NIH or other extramural funding; How your work would align with one or more of the interdisciplinary research strengths described in the position overview; How you anticipate using or contributing to Boise State’s CORE facilities; and Your approach to mentoring researchers, including undergraduate students, graduate students, or postdoctoral researchers, as applicable. 4) Teaching Statement (two page maximum), describing: Your teaching and mentoring experience; Your approach to supporting student learning and addressing barriers to learning; How you have or plan to assess and improve your teaching; and How you would contribute to the department’s instructional needs and collaborate with colleagues. 5) Representative Publications: One PDF containing three representative publications or, if needed due to file-size limitations, a single document with links to the publications. Please select works that demonstrate your research accomplishments and future potential. Please note that the application system accepts up to five documents, with a maximum file size of 10 MB each. Please plan accordingly to ensure all required materials are included. If the three representative publications cannot be combined within the file-size limit, you may provide links to them in a single uploaded document. Please also provide contact information for three professional references, including names, phone numbers, and email addresses. Reference information will be entered directly into the application system and does not need to be uploaded as a separate document. Closing Date: Position will close for new applicants on October 26, 2026 For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Javier Ochoa-Reparaz (jochoareparaz@boisestate.edu ) and Dr. Eric Hayden (erichayden@boisestate.edu) Salary and Benefits: Starting salary: The 9-month academic year salary ranges from $75,000 to $80,000. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d4910a19 Last Name (required) 2fdef00d Email (required) 630f2d1f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 665ab16a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) e3d4c75e Last Name (required) c7c55c44 Email (required) 33df318e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
    },
    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-biological-sciences-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Biological Sciences",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor, Biological Sciences - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor, Biological Sciences Assistant Teaching Professor, Biological Sciences 499864 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Sep 25 2026 Closing on: Oct 26 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Boise State University’s Department of Biological Sciences invites applicants for a full-time Assistant Teaching Professor (non-tenure track) position. Although non-tenure track, the position offers salary and promotion opportunities similar to those of tenure-track faculty, including advancement to associate and full teaching professor . The primary teaching duties will include lower division biology courses, such as Introductory Biology I: Cell and Molecular Biology, Anatomy and Physiology, Introductory Microbiology, or Introductory Biology II: Diversity of Life. The position may also include instruction of upper-division undergraduate courses such as Cell Biology or Molecular Biology lab. The workload assignment is approximately 80% teaching and 20% departmental service, which translates to the equivalent of four 3-credit classes each semester, with adjustments that take into account other workload factors such as class size. Teaching Faculty play a critical role in curriculum development. They manage laboratory courses and support the teaching of graduate student teaching assistants. They advance the University’s mission of providing student-centered, quality education and are committed to the success of our students and the university. Department Overview: The Department of Biological Sciences at Boise State University has a strong commitment to both research and teaching. Our department serves a large number of students majoring in biology, or taking biology courses for other degree programs. We share teaching experiences and strategies in order to improve the experiences of our students. Our department is committed to the success of our early career faculty and provides informal and formal mentoring. We strive to integrate research experiences in the classroom, and provide experiential learning for our students. Our curriculum is designed to support students in developing critical thinking and data analysis skills, laboratory expertise, scientific writing, and oral communication skills. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: A PhD in a field related to Biological Sciences, such as Genetics, Cell and Molecular Biology, Biochemistry, Microbiology, Physiology, or General Biology. Preferred qualifications: An interest in developing and delivering undergraduate curriculum. A commitment to monitoring and improving teaching and thoughtful course design using evidence-based practices. A commitment to creating inclusive teaching environments where all students can succeed. Prior teaching or mentorship experience in the biological sciences. Required Application Materials: Cover letter Two page maximum Provide a synopsis of why you are interested in this position, your relevant experiences, and your qualifications Curriculum vitae Employment history (including dates of employment) Relevant teaching or mentorship experience (courses taught, course development, mentorship roles) Professional activities including service and professional development in teaching Statement of teaching (two page maximum) that describes: How you implement evidence-based instructional practices How your teaching supports the success of all students How you create an inclusive classroom environment How you monitor and improve your courses A description of how you would approach teaching a ~150 person 100-level Introductory Cell and Molecular Biology course Transcripts (unofficial is OK) from all undergraduate and graduate coursework Please also provide contact information for three professional references, including names, phone numbers, and email addresses. Reference information will be entered directly into the application system and does not need to be uploaded as a separate document. Closing Date: The position will close for new applicants on October 26, 2026. For questions regarding this position, please contact Dr. Emily Meredith (emilymeredith@boisestate.edu). Salary and Benefits: Starting salary of $65,000. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) aa5c69c6 Last Name (required) 7e5c1cb6 Email (required) fc14e29f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert fcbade66 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 4425ff4f Last Name (required) 30fdd0be Email (required) 6aa144a7 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
