    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-english-teaching-writing-studies-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - English Teaching, Writing Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - English Teaching, Writing Studies - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - English Teaching, Writing Studies Assistant Professor - English Teaching, Writing Studies 499881 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Sep 25 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Department of Writing Studies at Boise State University invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor of English Teaching, beginning in August 2027. We seek a teacher-scholar with expertise in English education and experience teaching English Language Arts in grades 6–12. The successful candidate will contribute to the preparation of future English educators, maintain an active research program, and participate in service to the department, university, profession, and broader educational community. Primary teaching responsibilities will include undergraduate English Language Arts methods courses and other courses that support the department’s English Teaching major. The successful candidate will have opportunities to shape curriculum, mentor and advise preservice teachers, and build partnerships with schools and educators throughout the region. This position also offers meaningful opportunities to work with educators across the career span. The faculty member may contribute to the Boise State Writing Project and collaborate with colleagues, practicing teachers, and community partners to strengthen the teaching of writing and English Language Arts. We welcome candidates whose teaching and scholarship will advance the department’s commitment to preparing reflective, knowledgeable, and responsive educators. Department overview: The Department of Writing Studies houses two undergraduate programs: English Teaching and Professional & Public Writing . DWS thrives on a culture of curiosity, collaboration, and creativity. Our faculty actively engage in campus and community partnerships, creating opportunities for students to apply their coursework to meaningful, real-world experiences. We are a supportive community of teacher-scholars who value pedagogical innovation and student-centered practice. About the English Teaching Program The English Teaching program prepares educators to cultivate classrooms grounded in dialogue and inquiry, empowering young people through the English Language Arts. Guided by our values—collaboration, inquiry, growth, possibility, and community—our program takes an asset-based approach to preparing middle and high school teachers. Leading to ELA certification in grades 6–12, our curriculum integrates methods coursework with field-based experiences and local classroom mentorship. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop: a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: PhD or EdD in English education, literacy education, curriculum and instruction with a focus on English Language Arts, literacy, or a related field Experience teaching English Language Arts in grades 6-12 in the United States Preferred qualifications: Experience teaching preservice teachers Record of research/scholarship Demonstrated commitment to student-centered, dialogic, and asset-based pedagogical approaches Required application materials: Cover letter CV Teaching philosophy statement Research statement Contact information for three professional references Closing Date: Position will remain open until filled, with review to begin on December 7, 2026. For questions regarding this position, please contact Amber Warrington, amberwarrington@boisestate.edu . Salary and Benefits: Salary starts at $61,000 and is commensurate with experience. Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contracts and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 17b0fda2 Last Name (required) 77f0015c Email (required) 894c2a52 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6b9e5a8a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 960f14b1 Last Name (required) 7a48df40 Email (required) 9e09c1e4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
