    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/lecturer-chemistry-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Lecturer - Chemistry",
      "description": "Lecturer - Chemistry - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Lecturer - Chemistry Lecturer - Chemistry 499813 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Aug 11 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position overview: The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Boise State University invites applications for a full-time Lecturer position. The successful candidate will contribute to the department’s teaching mission with primary teaching responsibilities in freshman and sophomore courses with the possibility of upper-division courses within their area of disciplinary expertise. Course assignments will include general chemistry and may also include discipline-specific courses that align with departmental needs and the candidate’s background. Summer teaching opportunities may be available for additional compensation. Lecturers teach four courses per semester and are integral members of the department’s instructional team. The department is committed to delivering high-quality, engaging undergraduate education and values innovative, evidence-based teaching practices that promote student learning and success. These practices may include active learning strategies, the use of modern laboratory instrumentation, and technology-enhanced instruction. The department also supports professional development and participation in initiatives that strengthen teaching effectiveness and enhance the student experience. Department overview: The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry offers Bachelor of Science and Master of Science degrees in Chemistry. The department's vision is to “Promote student success through excellence in chemistry.” We realize this vision by providing exceptional student research experiences and a curriculum designed to develop critical-thinking skills, independent research projects, instrumentation training, exceptional laboratory practices, and mastery of scientific writing. As a Carnegie-classified R2 institution (Ph.D. granting, high research activity), we are dedicated to increasing high impact research. Our faculty members conduct research in areas such as drug discovery, medicinal chemistry and medical devices, cosmochemistry, prebiotic chemistry, archaeological science, computational chemistry, enzymology and enzyme mechanisms, RNA and protein chemistry, and polymer chemistry. Our faculty members participate in transdisciplinary programs and mentor M.S. and Ph.D. students in transdisciplinary programs including Materials Science and Engineering, Biomolecular Sciences, Biomedical Engineering, and Computing. We are proud of our collaborative culture and shared commitment to cooperation, collegiality, and respect . About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital – a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We’re nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty members are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers the perfect backdrop – a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about faculty careers at Boise State and living in the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: Master’s degree in chemistry, biochemistry, chemistry education, science education, or a closely related field. Candidates whose graduate degree is in an education-related field must also hold a bachelor’s degree in chemistry or biochemistry Preferred qualifications: Ph.D. in chemistry, biochemistry, chemistry education, science education, or a closely related field Experience teaching general chemistry Experience developing and teaching online chemistry courses Experience using evidence-based instructional practices Demonstrated commitment to undergraduate student success Experience using modern laboratory instrumentation or technology-enhanced teaching methods Required application materials: Cover letter describing the applicant’s interest in the position and relevant qualifications Curriculum vitae or résumé Statement of teaching philosophy Contact information for three professional references Closing Date: Review of applications will begin on September 27, 2026. For questions regarding this position, please contact Brian McClain, brianmcclain@boisestate.edu Salary and Benefits: Salary ranges from $56,000 to $61,000 and is commensurate with experience Our standard faculty contract is a 9-month contract (unless otherwise noted) with pay and benefits spread over 12 months. This is a yearly, renewable contract, unless noted that the position is temporary. More information about faculty contract and work days is available here . Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package , including (but not limited to): 10.76% University contribution to your ORP retirement fund (Professional and Faculty employees) Excellent medical, dental and other health-related insurance coverages Tuition fee waiver benefits for employees, spouses and their dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 71b7f009 Last Name (required) 4aa60896 Email (required) 06da6f08 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert b0c7f48b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) 3dc73219 Last Name (required) f9a77c00 Email (required) a2a28195 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
