    "https://jobs.boisestate.edu/jobs/assistant-teaching-professor-communication-boise-idaho-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Communication",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Communication - Boise, Idaho, United States Back to Boise State My Profile Kiosk mode Assistant Teaching Professor - Communication Assistant Teaching Professor - Communication 499856 Boise, Idaho Faculty Opening on: Sep 22 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Boise State University Department of Communication invites applications for an Assistant Teaching Professor (annually renewable contract, eligible for promotion) to begin Fall 2027. Ideal candidates will bring excitement and enthusiasm in their approach to teaching our core curriculum—COMM 248: Communication Perspectives and COMM 298: Communication Inquiries—while continuing to help broaden our existing departmental strengths. We seek candidates with teaching expertise that fits within at least one of our three areas of curricular focus: Culture & Advocacy Media & Society Social Systems For more information about our three areas of study and overall curriculum, view our Department of Communication Academic Catalog . Below is a general description of our two core classes: COMM 248: Communication Perspectives- This course is designed to support Communication majors in exploring various frameworks to study human communication that will guide their personal and professional lives. Students engage purposeful learning strategies to consider the value and possibilities of the Communication field, including degree planning and career development. The course provides students foundational opportunities to build community with other Communication majors at the start of their degree program. COMM 298: Communication Inquiries- This course introduces students to the theoretical and practical uses of multiple communication research methods. The student will learn how to conduct background research, develop research questions and hypotheses, design research projects, collect/analyze data, and present results. They will also see research in action through reading various studies. Standard position responsibilities include a 4/4 teaching load with service expectations. We offer mentoring and departmental resources to foster successful teaching activities. We are looking for colleagues with complementary interests who will help maintain and enhance our vibrant major by partnering and collaborating with faculty and students within our department and across campus. Candidates should have a strong commitment to student success, collaborative governance, inclusive mentoring, and undergraduate teaching. Department overview: The Department of Communication offers B.A. degrees to approximately 400 students, making it one of the largest departments in the College of Arts and Sciences. Our faculty demonstrate a commitment to both teaching and research excellence, featuring innovative pedagogical practices, publication records in top-tier journals, and active engagement in communication and interdisciplinary associations. About Boise State: Boise State University is a powerhouse of creativity, research, and impact. Our campus sits along the Boise River and reaches into the heart of Idaho’s capital—a vibrant hub for innovation, culture, and outdoor adventure. We are nationally recognized for trailblazing research, student success, and community impact. Our faculty are scholars, mentors, and changemakers who advance ideas, discoveries, and the next generation of leaders. Boise offers a welcoming city with a thriving arts scene, a growing tech sector, and mountains on the horizon. Join us and help shape a bold, collaborative academic community. Learn more about Faculty Careers at Boise State and the City of Boise . Minimum qualifications: A terminal degree appropriate to the field of Communication; or A master’s degree in Communication or a closely related field and at least eight years of full-time teaching experience at the college or university level or equivalent professional experience in the discipline. Demonstrated expertise and teaching experience in Communication. For purposes of this position, equivalent experience may include professional training, curriculum development, instructional leadership, or other substantial professional work that includes responsibility for teaching or facilitating learning in communication-related settings. Required application materials: Cover Letter: Outlines candidate interest in the position and addresses: Approach to teaching in our core curriculum (COMM 248 / COMM 298) Alignment/fit within one or more of our three curricular focus areas Curriculum Vitae: Details employment history, publications (if applicable), courses taught, leadership roles, and professional service. Teaching Portfolio: (as separate uploaded documents) Teaching Philosophy Sample Syllabus Sample Assignment including its learning objectives and assessment approach References: Contact information for three professional references will be collected as part of the application; they do not need to be uploaded as a freestanding document Reference Procedure We will conduct phone/Zoom reference checks from your listed references later in the candidate review process. References will receive automated requests via email at that time. Formal letters of recommendation are not required upon initial application. Closing Date: This position will remain open until filled, with review of applications to begin on October 21st, 2026. Inquiries may be addressed to the Search Committee Chair, Dr. Matt Isbell (matthewisbell@boisestate.edu). Salary and Benefits: Salary: $58,500 – $61,000 (9-month, renewable teaching faculty appointment; non-tenure track, eligible for promotion). Benefits: Boise State University provides a best-in-class benefits package, including: 10.76% University contribution to an ORP retirement fund Comprehensive medical, dental, and health insurance options Tuition fee waivers for employees, spouses, and dependents Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners Explore our full Boise State Benefits Page for details. Dual Career Assistance Support for spouses and partners. See our full benefits page for more information Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 9e744597 Last Name (required) 04d015ee Email (required) ac5ff064 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Associate Director, Ticket Operations Boise, Idaho Administration and Business Operations, Athletics, Management, Mid-Level Assistant Teaching Professor of Jazz Studies Boise, Idaho College of Arts & Sciences Assistant Professor, Public Policy and Administration Boise, Idaho College of Education and Public Service Equal Employment Opportunity Boise State University is committed to providing equal employment opportunities to all employees and qualified applicants for employment as provided for by federal, state, and local law. The university does not discriminate in employment opportunities or actions on the basis of any status or class protected under applicable federal, state, or local law. The University endeavors to recruit, hire, train, and promote the most qualified employees in all job titles. All other personnel actions are administered without regard to protected class under federal, state, or local law. If you require an accommodation at any step in our recruitment process, you are encouraged to contact (208) 426-1616 or hr@boisestate.edu. Jeanne Clery Act Each year, Boise State University prepares an Annual Security Report and Annual Fire Safety Report as part of the University's commitment to safety and security on campus and in compliance with the Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Police and Crime Statistics Act. The report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on the main Boise State campus, all of Boise State's separate campuses, in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Boise State, and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from Boise State's campuses. Also included in the report are the University's institutional policies and procedures concerning campus security, including those related to sexual assault, campus alerts, drug and alcohol use, and others. You can obtain a copy of the report by accessing the following website or you can request a copy of the report by contacting the University's Department of Public Safety at 2245 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83706; by calling 208-426-6911; or by sending an email to publicsafety@boisestate.edu. Annual Security and Fire Safety Report Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 6e69f045 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences Employment Type Faculty Faculty Locations Boise, Idaho, United States Boise, Idaho, United States First Name (required) d4cd6c1a Last Name (required) a9d2b803 Email (required) d68ae37e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Boise State University (208) 426-1000 1910 University Drive, Boise, Idaho 83725 Facebook Instagram X Youtube LinkedIn Cookie Preferences Terms of Use Accessibility Privacy © 2026 All Rights Reserved. Boise State University Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
